   "id": 103,
   "body": "In Q3, how do I use $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$ when the car stops?",
   "image": null,
   "mine": true,
   "sender_id": "0ae3e33c-3ded-41c4-931f-a42e0b3f4138",
   "client_ref": "",
   "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:27:15.445534Z"
  },
  {
   "id": 104,
   "body": "When it stops, final velocity $v = 0$. So $0 = u^2 + 2as$, then $s = -\\frac{u^2}{2a}$.",
   "image": null,
   "mine": false,
   "sender_id": "5314ab58-c2bc-462c-a9d1-65283d8f73b5",
   "client_ref": "",
   "created_at": "2026-10-21T17:25:15.445534Z"
  },
  {
   "id": 105,
   "body": "Remember $a$ is negative because it slows down.",
   "image": null,
   "mine": false,
   "sender_id": "5314ab58-c2bc-462c-a9d1-65283d8f73b5",
   "client_ref": "",
   "created_at": "2026-10-21T17:26:15.445534Z"
  },
  {
   "id": 106,
   "body": "Got it, thank you Sir!",
